 "description": "Two experiments at one site over the same rows, and the baseline they share. `interventions` declares interchange patching and mean ablation at the last position of layer 0; nothing there runs until a step lists it. `clean` runs the un-intervened model, scores it, and reads the activation `mean` averages. `patched` lists `patching`, whose operand is `counterfactual.v_cf`; `ablated` lists `ablation`, whose operand is `mean`, the step before it. Each metric is a step with its own name, `patching_ld` and `ablation_ld`, so the two experiments' results sit side by side in one output directory and `plan.table(\"patching_ld\", \"ablation_ld\")` joins them row by row. Tiny CPU Llama, so the numbers demonstrate the mechanism and nothing else.",
